# Public Supabase config — safe to commit.
# The anon key is designed to be exposed to the browser; all data access is
# governed by Row Level Security. The SERVICE ROLE key is NOT here and must
# NEVER be committed or prefixed with VITE_ (it bypasses RLS).
#
# Vite loads this .env for every build (including Lovable/Vercel). Local dev
# can still override these in the gitignored .env.local.
# Google Maps JavaScript API key — used ONLY by AddressAutocomplete for
# address suggestions. Public by design: it ships in the client bundle, so
# anyone can read it. What protects it is the HTTP-referrer restriction in
# Google Cloud (ccsta.net only) plus the API restriction to Maps
# JavaScript + Places. If those are ever removed, this key is abusable.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=AIzaSyAVvp-Wk4osKJTHlkSnHJ6DMyT2G00Aeps

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://wurnsxgvmpabfchzeyrz.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_g4vm1crP0gNKiiZmFu82FA_DaR7XpTb

